  "result": "Original construction and existing-property update gates fail before and pass afterward with unchanged measured charges. At 16000 properties end-to-end construction plus for-in improves 38.2x; at 16384 properties repeated updates improve 311.9x. Dispatch controls include slowdowns up to 5.3%; fresh realm controls remain within 1%. These medians are not statistical significance claims.",
  "limitations": "Indexes are derived and lazily built on long-chain misses; successful lookups return immediately without probing later suffixes. A write-path membership vector grows to the highest indexed slot, like the arena liveness metadata. Intrinsic installation still scans function metadata; this removes name-table rescans, not all possible realm-size-dependent work."
